   "title": "Police raid justice ministry, prosecution over alleged records leak to lawmaker",
   "url": "https://www.koreatimes.co.kr/southkorea/politics/20261127/police-raid-justice-ministry-prosecution-over-alleged-records-leak-to-lawmaker",
   "domain": "koreatimes.co.kr",
   "source": "koreatimes.co.kr",
   "published": "Fri, 27 Nov 2026 04:52:03 GMT",
   "_dt": 1795755123.0,
   "ageDays": 0.01,
   "summary": "Police on Friday raided the justice ministry and prosecution offices over allegations that investigative records were leaked to independent lawmaker Han Dong-hoon. The Seoul Metropolitan Police Agency sent investigators to search the ministry, the Supreme Prosecutors Office and the Seoul Western District Prosecutors Office and secure evidence related to the allegations.",
   "summary_zh": "警方于周五突袭韩国司法部和检察机关，原因是有人指控调查记录被泄露给独立议员韩东勋。首尔 Metropolitan Police Agency 派出调查人员搜查司法部、最高人民检察院和首尔西部地方检察机关，以获取与相关指控有关的证据。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Police on Friday raided the justice ministry and prosecution offices over allegations that investigative records were leaked to independent lawmaker Han Dong-hoon. The Seoul Metropolitan Police Agency sent investigators to search the ministry, the Supreme Prosecutors Office and the Seoul Western District Prosecutors Office and secure evidence related to the allegations. The ruling Democratic Party of Korea filed a complaint against Han in September on suspicion of disclosing official secrets after he raised lobbying allegations against then Justice Minister nominee Kim Seung-won. Han at the time unveiled a prosecution report about Kim's lobbying allegations, drawing questions over how he obtained the document. Kim later withdrew his candidacy amid growing controversy over the scandal",
