   "title": "Shettima Praises Otti, Other South-East Governors Over Performance",
   "url": "https://leadership.ng/shettima-praises-otti-other-south-east-governors-over-performance/",
   "domain": "leadership.ng",
   "source": "Leadership（尼日利亚）",
   "published": "Fri, 27 Nov 2026 04:35:25 +0000",
   "_dt": 1795754125.0,
   "ageDays": 0.03,
   "summary": "While commending Soludo for his administration’s urban renewal projects, the Vice-President singled out Otti for praise, noting that political affiliation should not determine the recognition of good governance. Shettima also commended Ebonyi State Governor, Francis Nwifuru, for his performance, describing his Imo State counterpart as a great politician and builder of roads and people.",
   "summary_zh": "副总统在赞扬索卢多推进城市更新项目的同时，特别表扬了奥蒂，并指出，政党归属不应成为认可良好治理的标准。谢蒂马还赞扬了埃博尼州州长弗朗西斯·恩维富鲁的施政表现，称这位伊莫州州长是一位杰出的政治家，也是一位道路和民生建设者。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "The projects included the Ekwulobia Flyover Bridge, Tower of Light, shopping mall and ancillary structures. While commending Soludo for his administration’s urban renewal projects, the Vice-President singled out Otti for praise, noting that political affiliation should not determine the recognition of good governance. “Governor Alex Otti was elected on the platform of the Labour Party, but he is doing wonderfully well. We must give credit where it is due,” he said. Shettima also commended Ebonyi State Governor, Francis Nwifuru, for his performance, describing his Imo State counterpart as a great politician and builder of roads and people. He also praised Enugu State Governor, Peter Mbah, for his efforts to address the state’s longstanding water supply challenges. According to him, Mbah demonstrated foresight by securing a loan from Zenith Bank and importing water pipes even before his inauguration, a move he said was beginning to improve access to pipe-borne water in the state. The Vice-President urged the people of the South-East to participate actively in national politics, stressing that the region’s importance to Nigeria should not be limited by ethnic considerations. “Ndigbo are too important to Nigeria to be confined to a tribal cocoon,” he said. He described Soludo as a courageous leader with strong convictions, commending him and the All Progressives Grand Alliance (APGA) for aligning with President Bola Tinubu’s Renewed Hope Agenda. Shettima said the partnership was already producing results in Anambra, citing the commissioned projects as evidence of the state’s development efforts. He described Soludo as the best governor in Anambra’s contemporary history and expressed confidence that his political career would extend beyond the governorship. The Vice-President urged Anambra residents to support Soludo’s administration through prayers, ideas and payment of taxes and levies. “Every naira honestly paid in revenue contributes to the roads, hospitals, schools and other public infrastructure that improve your lives,” he said. He also urged residents to protect public infrastructure against vandalism, maintain clean streets and ensure that trading activities did not obstruct roads and the flyover. “These facilities belong to you, and their future is in your hands. Remember, a governor can build a bridge, but only the people can keep it standing,” he said. Earlier, Soludo said the projects were part of his administration’s commitment to transforming Anambra into a liveable and prosperous state where residents could enjoy better living conditions and pursue their economic activities. The commissioning ceremony attracted several prominent personalities, including businessman, Sir Emeka Offor; Cardinal Peter Okpaleke; Chairman of the Anambra State Traditional Rulers Council, Igwe Chidubem Iweka III; and former Ohanaeze Ndigbo National Vice-President, Ichie Damian Okeke-Ogene. Others included APGA National Chairman, Chief Sly Ezeokenwa; the party’s Anambra State Chairman, Chief Ifeatu Obi-Okoye; former Senator Uche Ekwunife; and APGA chieftains, Chief Ben Obi and Chief Titus. We’ve got the edge. Get real-time reports, breaking scoops, and exclusive angles delivered straight to your phone. Don’t settle for stale news. Join LEADERSHIP NEWS on WhatsApp for 24/7 updates → Join Our WhatsApp Channel --> --> Previous Post AbdulRazaq Flags Off APC Campaign In Kwara South, Rolls Out Achievements Okechukwu Obeta Obeta Boniface Okechukwu is a Senior Reporter at Leadership Newspaper with more than 30 years of journalism experience. His reporting spans politics, crime, the judiciary, culture, human rights, and accountability in governance. He is recognised for factual, engaging reporting and a strong commitment to ethical journalism that has earned him a reputation as a reliable and authoritative voice",
