   "published": "Thu, 26 Nov 2026 10:37:02 GMT",
   "_dt": 1795689422.0,
   "ageDays": 0.77,
   "summary": "Kookmin University co-hosts conference commemorating independence activist Scholars from Korea, China and Japan will gather Friday for an international academic conference commemorating Korean independence activist Ahn Jung-geun. The conference will be co-hosted by Kookmin University and the Korea-China Civilian Standing Committee for the Search for Ahn Jung-geun, with support from the Ministry of Patriots and Veterans Affairs.",
   "summary_zh": "国民大学联合主办纪念独立运动活动者的会议：来自韩国、中国和日本的学者将于周五举行一场国际学术会议，纪念韩国独立运动活动者安重根。此次会议由国民大学与韩中安重根查明真相和平民间联合委员会共同主办，并得到韩国祖国和退伍军人事务部的支持。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Kookmin University co-hosts conference commemorating independence activist Scholars from Korea, China and Japan will gather Friday for an international academic conference commemorating Korean independence activist Ahn Jung-geun. The conference will be co-hosted by Kookmin University and the Korea-China Civilian Standing Committee for the Search for Ahn Jung-geun, with support from the Ministry of Patriots and Veterans Affairs. The conference will open with an address by Chung Sye-kyun, chairman of the Ahn Jung-geun Memorial Association, followed by remarks from Jung Tae-ho, co-chair of the National Assembly Caucus for the Exhumation and Repatriation of Ahn Jung-geun’s Remains. Kwon Oh-eul, minister of patriots and veterans affairs, will deliver a welcoming speech, followed by opening remarks from Hwang Ki-chul, chairman of the civilian committee. “At this conference, we plan to compare and analyze the perspectives of Korea, China and Japan on Ahn Jung-geun’s martyrdom in 1910, drawing on contemporary sources to trace the historical development of commemorations honoring him,” said Hwang Sun-ik, a professor in Kookmin University’s Department of Korean History. “I hope the conference will help uncover clues that could lead to the exhumation and repatriation of Ahn’s remains,” added Hwang, who also heads the university’s Institute of Korean Studies. Ahn Jung-geun assassinated Ito Hirobumi, a former Japanese prime minister and resident-general of Korea, in Harbin, China, in 1909. He was later imprisoned and executed by Japanese authorities at Lushun Prison in 1910",
